# zen-free sidecar — account wiring (llmux side, manual)
#
# 1. Generate the shared key and put it in the router .env:
#      ZEN_API_KEY=oc-<hex>
#    This value is the Bearer token llmux will send as the account api_key.
#    It exists only inside the compose network — never publish zen-free's port.
#
# 2. Restart the sidecar so it picks up the env:
#      docker compose up -d --build zen-free
#    The sidecar writes its own api-keys.json on first boot (container-local,
#    git-ignored). The admin key inside that file MUST equal ZEN_API_KEY;
#    delete the file and restart if they ever drift apart.
#
# 3. In the llmux panel, create ONE account:
#      provider_id        zen-free
#      base_url           http://zen-free:6446/v1
#      chat_endpoint      http://zen-free:6446/v1
#      responses_endpoint http://zen-free:6446/v1
#      messages_endpoint  http://zen-free:6446/v1
#      api_key            <the same ZEN_API_KEY value>
#      default_protocol   chat
#      balance_provider   none        <-- required (see below)
#      openai_compatible  1
#
# 4. Create model aliases yourself (deliberately not automated):
#    chat-family ids (big-pickle, cat-jam-free, ling-3.1-flash-free,
#    mimo-v2.6-flash-free, ...) target Protocol::Chat;
#    muse-spark-*-contributor-free target Protocol::Responses (upstream_api=responses).
#    Model ids rot upstream — check GET http://zen-free:6446/v1/models for the
#    current fleet before binding an alias.
#
# Why balance_provider=none: the sidecar key is an intranet token. Any balance
# probe would carry it to opencode.ai and fail; disable probing like codex-api.

# Compose .env (router /root/docker/llmux/.env):
ZEN_API_KEY=oc-REPLACE_ME_WITH_HEX

# Sidecar env (compose sets these; listed here for reference):
# PROXY_PORT=6446
# KEYS_FILE=./api-keys.json            # container-local, git-ignored
# MODELS_CACHE_FILE=./models-cache.json # endpoint probe memory, git-ignored
# MODELS_TTL_MS=600000                 # /zen/v1/models refresh interval
#
# 注意 PROXY_HOST 刻意不设：默认 0.0.0.0 监听容器全部网卡，同一 compose 网络
# 的 llmux 才能连上。设成 127.0.0.1 会让 sidecar 只监听容器 loopback，连
# llmux 都够不着（这正是 codex-api 的配法 —— 它也没有 PROXY_HOST 这类变量）。
# 隔离靠 compose 不写 `ports:` 保证，外部到不了这个端口。
